Add Available Services toggle, APC tracking link, tidy order screen (v0.135)

Three asks from Dan:

1. New "Available Services" admin page for DPD and APC (Settings >
   Couriers > DPD/APC > Available services ->) - every service code
   either courier has actually offered so far, with a tick to control
   whether it still shows in the order screen's Service dropdown.
   Unticking (e.g. APC's Liquid codes BNS never uses) doesn't delete the
   code, just excludes it going forward via a new disabled-codes setting
   (apc_disabled_services/dpd_disabled_services) filtered out right
   before DpdShippingService/ApcShippingService return their service
   list - so it can be ticked again later, and never touches anything
   already booked. There's no fixed master catalog of every courier
   service code anywhere in this app, so the list is whatever's actually
   been seen live/cached so far, same as the dropdown itself already
   relies on.

2. APC tracking changed to open in a new tab via a plain link
   (apcTrackingUrl, mirroring dpdTrackingUrl), using the confirmed
   7-digit consignment number, instead of the previous in-page widget
   that called APC's authenticated Tracks API. The exact public URL
   format (apcchoice.apc-overnight.com/track-parcel?id=...&postcode=...)
   is a best-effort match to the tracker's own form fields - it's a
   client-rendered page, so it couldn't be confirmed end-to-end from this
   sandbox. Flagged clearly in code and the project's APC findings doc for
   Dan to confirm on the next real tracking click.

3. Removed two UI nudges on the order screen that were throwing off the
   layout: APC's "Type a product code manually instead" toggle, and the
   explanatory note under the Collection Service dropdown.

Also answered (no code change): why no Saturday-prefixed APC/DPD services
show up outside the right collection day - confirmed neither
ApcShippingService nor DpdShippingService does any day-of-week filtering
at all; the only date sent to either courier's service-lookup is today's
date (APC) or nothing (DPD), so which services come back is entirely
decided by the courier's own live API based on what their outbound
schedule actually offers for that collection day - testing on a Friday
is the right call.

